  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Leave the single market and customs union with a Great Repeal Bill and “no deal better than a bad deal”; reduce net migration to the tens of thousands; NHS funding of +£8bn; introduce an energy safeguard tariff cap; deliver 1.5m homes by 2022. TEXT_F: Seek a “jobs‑first” Brexit retaining Single Market/Customs Union benefits; managed migration without a numerical target; NHS over £30bn; £10 Living Wage and end zero‑hours contracts; rent caps and three‑year tenancies.",
